          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "MiCA stablecoin provisions required EU exchanges to delist non-approved tokens like USDT by hard compliance deadlines, setting a template for jurisdiction-driven forced delistings that will expand to other regions.",
          "source": "https://support.kraken.com/articles/stablecoin-offerings-for-eea-clients"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Exchange delisting authority is unilateral and legally opaque — Coinbase removed WBTC with no advance remedy path, prompting a $1B lawsuit that underscored how unchecked centralized venue gatekeeping is.",
          "source": "https://finst.com/en/blog/articles/delist-wbtc-and-steth"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Phased delistings of widely-held assets such as USDT across EU CASPs simultaneously compress on-chain liquidity pools, force asset migration at scale, and can reprice collateral positions across lending protocols.",
          "source": "https://www.binance.com/en/square/post/17787587546521"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Smaller-cap token delistings (SPELL, TRX on Binance US; IOTX under caution status) routinely cause sharp price dislocations as liquidity fragments across remaining venues with no guaranteed off-ramp.",
          "source": "https://sdlccorp.com/post/how-to-handle-delisting-of-tokens-on-crypto-exchange-platforms/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Counterparty / Legal",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Projects and custodians whose tokens are removed face asymmetric legal options — Bit Global's lawsuit against Coinbase ultimately settled, but the litigation risk deters smaller projects from challenging exchange decisions at all.",
